. 
. * Extract interaction term (female#treat_post)
. lincom 1.female#1.treat_post

 ( 1)  1.female#1.treat_post = 0

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
support_ge~2 | Coefficient  Std. err.      t    P>|t|     [95% conf. interval]
-------------+----------------------------------------------------------------
         (1) |   .0520853   .2975221     0.18   0.861    -.5310741    .6352447
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

. local coef_diff = r(estimate)

. local se_diff = r(se)

. 
. * Extract main effect for men (treat_post for female==0)
. lincom 1.treat_post

 ( 1)  1.treat_post = 0

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
support_ge~2 | Coefficient  Std. err.      t    P>|t|     [95% conf. interval]
-------------+----------------------------------------------------------------
         (1) |  -.2304804   .2353054    -0.98   0.327    -.6916918    .2307309
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

. local coef_male = r(estimate)

. 
. * Compute t-statistic and one-sided p-value for H1: male effect > female effe
> ct ⇔ coef_diff < 0
. local tstat_diff = -`coef_diff' / `se_diff'

. local pval_diff = ttail(e(df_r), `tstat_diff')

. 
. local interpretation "positive coefficient is in line with hypothesis"

. local family "t"

. 
. 
. * Output to file
. local N = e(N)

. local num_participants = e(N_g)  // Number of individuals

. 
. file open myfile using "$OUT/h4_results.csv", write replace
